# {{ site.title }}: {{ site.tagline }}

> {{ site.description }}

The chain is ticket → spec → verified pull request, with the spec and every decision recorded in the repository next to the code. Agent Smith is created and maintained by {{ site.author }}, who holds its copyright. Professional services, support and maintenance contracts are available from {{ site.partner }} ({{ site.partnerUrl }}).

Agent Smith is MIT licensed and runs on your own infrastructure. It reads tickets from Azure DevOps, Jira, GitHub Issues and GitLab Issues, works in Azure Repos, GitHub and GitLab repositories, and calls the AI provider you configure. A run derives specs from the ticket, implements them in sandboxes, checks every acceptance criterion with cited evidence, and opens one pull request per repository.

